    "result_text": "Full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a duplicate-email rejection to `POST /api/owners` that returns **409 Conflict** when the new owner's lower-cased email is already used by any other owner. To keep structural impact low, I followed the existing telephone-duplicate pattern with small, cohesive new units rather than growing any existing function:\n\n**New files (each a tiny single-method class):**\n- `RejectDuplicateOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 the pipeline step; skips the optional/blank email, else compares this owner's (already lower-cased) email against every other owner's lower-cased email and throws.\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java` \u2014 checked escalation.\n- `DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409.\n- Escalation YAML mapping the exception to its handler.\n\n**One edited file:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `rejectDuplicateEmail` step right after `normalizeEmail` (so the compared email is already normalized/lower-cased) and before `rejectDuplicateTelephone`.\n\nNo existing function bodies were modified, so the only change-cost is the four-line YAML wiring insert. The new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass.",
